\ A recursion far deeper than the 64K boot stack. There is no guard page on bare metal, so running
\ past the stack writes over whatever the linker placed below it. The compiled entry check raises
\ instead, and the run ends through the failure exit.
\
\ A shallow run of the same word goes first, so the serial output shows the recursion itself works
\ and it is the depth that fails. Nothing after the deep run executes. This runtime carries no
\ `recover`, so the raise ends the program.

deep: stack-recursive ( n -- n ) [ dup 0 > [ 1 - deep 1 + ] [ ] if ] ;

10 deep drop
"shallow recursion returned" print-line
1000000 deep drop
"unreachable" print-line
